    "AO": "",
    "AO\tCtrl+3": "",
    "Access collision object functions.  Collision objects are simple geometric primitives\nthat can be accessed via the SDK to assist with collision at run-time.\n\nHot key: 7 (toggles collision objects in the viewport)": "",
    "Access force functions.  Forces are modeling tools that manipulate growth in world-space.  Examples\nof their use include gravity (downward direction forces) and growing geometry around 3d\ngeometry (geometry forces)\n\nHot key: 6 (toggles forces in the viewport)": "",
    "Access high level wind functions.  Wind is controlled by a combination of properties in the\nmodel (typically in the 'Wind' group) and properties of the fan object.\n\nHot key: 8 (toggles wind)": "",
    "Add geometry to the model based on a set of predefined templates.  Once a template has been added,\nselect any of the new generators to edit the model.": "",
